From c7cfa432c13d1c4bab8bae4d27fbdadcfbca1a84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Date: Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:26:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: Fix runtime PM imbalance on error

The current code drops the runtime PM twice resulting in the error path
resulting in follow-up runtime PM imbalance:

spi_master spi2: noqueue transfer failed
rockchip-spi feb20000.spi: Runtime PM usage count underflow!

Fix the problem by always keeping the runtime PM count increased when
exiting __spi_pump_transfer_message(), as the caller handles decreasing
the count.

Note, that the function already had some other error paths where it
exits with the runtime PM count increased.

Signed-off-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Link: https://gitlab.collabora.com/hardware-enablement/rockchip-3588/linux/-/commit/c7cfa432c13d1c4bab8bae4d27fbdadcfbca1a84
---
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi.c b/drivers/spi/spi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi.c
@@ -1942,7 +1942,6 @@ static int __spi_pump_transfer_message(struct spi_controller *ctlr,
 	if (!was_busy && ctlr->auto_runtime_pm) {
 		ret = pm_runtime_get_sync(ctlr->dev.parent);
 		if (ret < 0) {
-			pm_runtime_put_noidle(ctlr->dev.parent);
 			dev_err(&ctlr->dev, "Failed to power device: %d\n",
 				ret);
 
@@ -1963,9 +1962,6 @@ static int __spi_pump_transfer_message(struct spi_controller *ctlr,
 				"failed to prepare transfer hardware: %d\n",
 				ret);
 
-			if (ctlr->auto_runtime_pm)
-				pm_runtime_put(ctlr->dev.parent);
-
 			msg->status = ret;
 			spi_finalize_current_message(ctlr);
 
